      "narrative": "Mara's brow furrows at your question. She picks up her wine, takes a slow sip, and sets it down again.\n\n\"Filed?\" She shakes her head, a faint crease between her brows. \"The lock wasn't filed, Kael. Toran replaced it \u2014 that's what I'm telling you. He swapped out the old mechanism for a new one a few months back. Standard rotation. Guild policy.\"\n\nShe taps a finger on the table.\n\n\"As for who removed the *original* lock \u2014 the one before Toran's \u2014 or who might have filed anything down...\" She shrugs, the motion flat and final. \"That'd be before my time. Before Toran's time, even. The Gate's been standing longer than either of us has been drawing breath.\"\n\nShe watches you, waiting to see if the answer lands.\n\n\"I can tell you who *replaced* the lock. That's Toran. That's in the ledgers. But the man who installed the first one, or whoever might've taken a file to it...\" She spreads her hands. \"Dead paperwork. Ash by now.\"\n\nA pause.\n\n\"Why do you ask about filing?\""
