      "narrative": "Mara's fingers still around her cup. She holds your gaze a beat longer this time, then sets the wine down with a decisive tap.\n\n\"Passage was never sold,\" she says flatly. \"The Ash Gate isn't a toll bridge. It's a Guild lock \u2014 Kestrel Guild controls it. They decide who crosses and when. Always have.\"\n\nShe ticks off on her fingers.\n\n\"The Guildmaster signs the writ. A courier carries it. Old Bram \u2014 the ferryman \u2014 he'd check the seal against a token held by the lockwright. Token matches seal, the lockwright opens the Gate, Bram rows you across. No coin ever changes hands. No bribes, no haggling.\"\n\nShe leans back, the chair creaking.\n\n\"If you're asking who the *lockwright* was \u2014 that's Toran Vex. If you're asking who *authorised* crossings \u2014 that's Guildmaster Aldric Vance, up in Thornfield.\" She gestures vaguely eastward. \"If you're asking who actually *used* the Gate...\" She spreads her hands. \"Ledgers. But those are locked in the Guild registry, and I don't have a key.\"\n\nShe watches you with those flint-grey eyes.\n\n\"Does that narrow it down, or does it raise more questions?\""
    },
