      "narrative": "You step closer to the Ash Gate, the damp gravel crunching under your boots. The mist coils lazily beyond the arch, the black river a low hush in the gully below. Nothing stirs.\n\nYou take a breath and call out.\n\n\"Old Bram!\"\n\nYour voice rings against the volcanic stone \u2014 sharp, clear \u2014 then fades into the fog. The echo bounces once off the gully wall and dies. No reply comes. Only the river's mutter and the drip of moisture from the arch's keystone.\n\nYou wait. Ten heartbeats. Twenty.\n\nThe mist swallows the silence whole. The satchel at the pillar's base sits undisturbed, its papers curling in the damp air. No boat scrapes against a distant shore. No voice calls back. No footsteps approach from the far side.\n\nThe Gate stays locked. The black water keeps its slow, patient course.\n\nWhoever Old Bram was, he isn't here to answer \u2014 and hasn't been for seven days."
    },
