      "narrative": "You crouch beside the satchel, your knee pressing into the damp earth. The leather is cold and clammy under your fingers, the snapped strap frayed at the break \u2014 cleanly torn, not cut. You lift the flap.\n\nInside, the satchel is nearly empty. A faint smell of old tobacco clings to the lining. Your fingers brush against something at the bottom \u2014 a small leather pouch, drawstring pulled tight. You tug it free. It clinks softly. Coin.\n\nYou loosen the drawstring and spill a few into your palm. Silver. A mix of Guild-stamped coins and older, worn pieces with edges smoothed by years of passing hands. A dozen or so, by feel. Not a fortune, but not nothing either.\n\nBeneath where the pouch sat, a crumpled square of parchment is wedged into the seam of the satchel's lining. You work it free with two fingers \u2014 it's soft, creased, the ink slightly smudged by damp. You unfold it.\n\nA map. Roughly drawn. A single line traces a route from a mark labelled *Ash Gate* through a series of jagged shapes \u2014 hills or mountains \u2014 to an X at the far end. No names. No notes. Just the line, the X, and a small symbol beside the X that you don't recognise: a circle with a line through its centre, like a crossed-out eye.\n\nThe mist shifts beyond the arch. The river keeps its low, patient sound.\n\nThe satchel holds nothing else."
    },
