      "narrative": "The Copper Finch's door groans open, and the warmth of the common room washes over you \u2014 woodsmoke, stale ale, the low murmur of morning conversation. A few heads turn, note your return, and look away. You cross to the scarred table near the window \u2014 your table \u2014 and sit.\n\nThe wood is pitted with old knife marks and candle wax. Through the grimy pane, the Ash Gate is a black sliver against the grey horizon.\n\nA few moments pass. The fire crackles. A serving girl wipes a mug behind the bar. Then a shadow falls across your table.\n\nMara Venn stands there, charcoal coat buttoned to her throat, a fresh cup of wine in one hand. She doesn't ask permission \u2014 she pulls out the chair across from you and sits, the legs scraping against the floorboards.\n\n\"Back already,\" she says, not a question. Her eyes flick to your hands, to the empty tabletop. \"The Gate's still sealed, I take it. Did you find anything out there worth the mud on your boots?\""
